:: Widgets DoLX Changelog [widget]
<<widget "DoLXChangelog">>
	<div class="changelog-overlay">
		<div class="changelog-hero">
			<span class="changelog-hero-icon" aria-hidden="true">&#128220;</span>
			<div>
				<div class="changelog-label">PATCH NOTES</div>
				<h1>DoL X-Change <span>v0.22.2a</span></h1>
				<div class="changelog-apk-note"><strong>Official X-Change APK:</strong> Join the DoL Modding server and check the dedicated <a href="https://discord.com/channels/675158131688603721/1512272787572785162" target="_blank">X-Change Channel</a>.</div>
			</div>
		</div>
		<a class="changelog-release-link" href="https://gitgud.io/Akoz/dol-xchange/-/releases" target="_blank"><span aria-hidden="true">&#128279;</span> View the full changelog and all releases <span aria-hidden="true">&#8599;</span></a>
		<h2><span class="changelog-section-icon new" aria-hidden="true">&#10022;</span> Changes and Additions</h2>
		<ul>
		<li><strong>Added Dragon Boost for Water Dragons</strong>
			<ul>
			<li>Water Dragons at transformation level 2+ can use <strong>Dragon Boost</strong> once per non-consensual encounter.
			</li>
			<li>Curl up and ram one attacker at full strength.
			</li>
			<li>Each ram has a <strong>10% chance to instantly knock out</strong> the target.
			</li>
			<li>In group fights, only the rammed enemy is knocked out.
			</li>
			</ul>
		</li>
		<li><strong>Added an optional unfamiliar-body adjustment period</strong>
			<ul>
			<li>Body changes from X-Change pills, or changing back afterwards, can temporarily lower <strong>Physique, Athletics, Swimming, Dancing, and Skulduggery</strong>.
			</li>
			<li>The longer the previous body was kept, the stronger and longer the penalty.
			</li>
			<li>Less than 2 days gives no penalty, so frequent NOW-pill switching is unaffected.
			</li>
			<li>Staying in one body for 2 months or more can cause up to a <strong>30% penalty</strong> that fades over 2 weeks.
			</li>
			<li>The effect appears on the Characteristics screen as <strong>unfamiliar body</strong>.
			</li>
			<li>Disabled by default under <strong>X-Change Settings &gt; Pill Behaviour</strong>.
			</li>
			</ul>
		</li>
		<li><strong>Added a new X-Change dream: First Orgasm</strong>
			<ul>
			<li>After the first orgasm in a swapped body, the player may dream about it that night.
			</li>
			<li>On waking, choose to feel unchanged, accept the body, or fully embrace it as the new self.
			</li>
			<li>Acceptance choices require Gender Identity to be enabled.
			</li>
			<li>Also fixes the Classic body type's flat chest and Harper's vanilla-sprite positioning.
			</li>
			<li>Contributed by <strong>Akoz (MR !44)</strong>.
			</li>
			</ul>
		</li>
		<li><strong>Expanded Robin's confession</strong>
			<ul>
			<li>Robin's confession can now be rejected after reading the note.
			</li>
			<li>The player can say they only want to be friends and mention existing love interests.
			</li>
			<li>Robin reacts badly but remains a friend.
			</li>
			<li>After one week, the player can still change their mind, accept the confession, or ask Robin to become sexfriends.
			</li>
			<li>Fixed Robin sometimes getting stuck in post-breakup mode when several days pass at once.
			</li>
			</ul>
		</li>
		<li><strong>Expanded blackmail</strong>
			<ul>
			<li>Added Blackmail Quest 17 for characters with previous chef experience.
			</li>
			<li>Requires a waiter/waitress shift followed by making a bodily-fluid cream bun.
			</li>
			<li>The waiter shift redirects the quest into the chef route.
			</li>
			<li>Completion is recorded only after the fluid bun is successfully made.
			</li>
			</ul>
		</li>
		<li><strong>Gwylan can ask their puppy for relief</strong>
			<ul>
			<li>During petplay, Gwylan can ask for relief when pent up and the player is wearing a collar.
			</li>
			<li>The player can accept or refuse with no penalty for refusing.
			</li>
			<li>With watersports enabled and high Yearning, Gwylan may also want to mark the player afterwards.
			</li>
			<li>Can happen at most once per week.
			</li>
			</ul>
		</li>
		<li><strong>You can now unmask the brown fox</strong>
			<ul>
			<li>The player can identify the brown fox as Gwylan even without the leg-wound or hypnosis hints.
			</li>
			<li>Available at the pub or Gwylan's shop after the Skyscraper.
			</li>
			<li>Requires at least <strong>50% Gwylan Love</strong> and <strong>400 Skulduggery</strong>.
			</li>
			</ul>
		</li>
		<li><strong>Added more chest control during sex</strong>
			<ul>
			<li>Added <strong>Pull away</strong> when someone has their mouth on the player's chest.
			</li>
			<li>During consensual sex, they stop and will not go for the chest again unless offered.
			</li>
			<li>During non-consensual encounters, it becomes a Willpower check that pushes them back one step.
			</li>
			<li><strong>Push towards their mouth</strong> now works while kissing and breaks the kiss first.
			</li>
			</ul>
		</li>
		<li><strong>Added post-bath clothing choices at Avery's mansion</strong>
			<ul>
			<li>After bathing alone, choose to dress as before, wrap in a towel, put on a bathrobe if available, or stay naked and send the clothes to the mansion wardrobe.
			</li>
			</ul>
		</li>
		<li><strong>Added waterproof makeup</strong>
			<ul>
			<li>Every lipstick, eyeshadow, and blusher colour now has a waterproof version at the cosmetics shop.
			</li>
			<li>Added waterproof concealer for hiding freckles.
			</li>
			<li>Remove it through the mirror.
			</li>
			</ul>
		</li>
		<li><strong>Console: new Fruit game, improved Virtual Pet, and challenges</strong>
			<ul>
			<li>Added a new <strong>Fruit game</strong> to the bedroom console.
			</li>
			<li>Drop and merge matching fruit into larger ones, up to a watermelon, while keeping the pile below the red line.
			</li>
			<li>Added <strong>Classic, Arcade, and Zen</strong> modes.
			</li>
			<li>Arcade adds combos and power-ups, while Zen has no game over.
			</li>
			<li>Fruit includes a tutorial, statistics, unlockable jar themes, appearance/audio settings, and saved runs.
			</li>
			<li><strong>Fruit, Virtual Pet, and Outbreak now all have challenges and daily challenges</strong>.
			</li>
			<li>Daily challenges reset at midnight UTC and reward <strong>£200–£500</strong> depending on difficulty.
			</li>
			<li>Completing every challenge unlocks a gold feat: <strong>Fruit Master</strong>, <strong>Champion Tamer</strong>, or <strong>Patient Zero</strong>.
			</li>
			<li>Fruit achievements can unlock additional jar themes.
			</li>
			<li>Virtual Pet challenge battles are practice only and do not affect pet stats.
			</li>
			<li>Virtual Pet now has unique animated pets and evolutions, animated battles, attacks, healing, bosses, and clearer menus.
			</li>
			<li>Outbreak now includes fixed challenge scenarios and a shared daily scenario.
			</li>
			<li>All three console games now have their own music and sound effects.
			</li>
			<li>Virtual Pet and Outbreak include new sounds for attacks, healing, buttons, events, and other actions.
			</li>
			<li>Console audio follows normal audio settings and bedroom music resumes after leaving the console.
			</li>
			</ul>
		</li>
		</ul>
		<h2><span class="changelog-section-icon fixes" aria-hidden="true">&#9874;</span> Tweaks and Rebalancing</h2>
		<ul>
		<li><strong>Colosseum fights now end by knockout</strong>
			<ul>
			<li>Opponent orgasms no longer end cage fights.
			</li>
			<li>Cage fights continue until someone is knocked out or the referee stops the fight due to Pain.
			</li>
			<li>Cage attacks deal more Pain based on rank, from <strong>x1.5 at F-rank/trial to x3 at S-rank</strong>.
			</li>
			<li>This stacks with the Enemy Damage Multiplier.
			</li>
			<li>Fights outside the cage are unchanged.
			</li>
			</ul>
		</li>
		<li><strong>Submissive and Defiant personality changes are more gradual</strong>
			<ul>
			<li>Moving back toward neutral is now half speed normally.
			</li>
			<li>It becomes quarter speed while the player has the Submissive, Bratty, or Defiant trait.
			</li>
			</ul>
		</li>
		<li><strong>Mate for Life now counts non-penetrative sex</strong>
			<ul>
			<li>Oral and tribbing can now count as long as the scene ends with a climax.
			</li>
			</ul>
		</li>
		</ul>
		<h2><span class="changelog-section-icon fixes" aria-hidden="true">&#9874;</span> Fixes and Improvements</h2>
		<ul>
		<li><strong>Fixed transformation feat boosts</strong>
			<ul>
			<li>Starting a new game no longer causes transformation feat boosts to break other selected boosts.
			</li>
			<li>Angel, Fallen Angel, Demon, and animal transformation boosts now work together correctly.
			</li>
			</ul>
		</li>
		<li><strong>Fixed Willpower feat boosts</strong>
			<ul>
			<li>Purchased Willpower now applies immediately.
			</li>
			<li>Willpower checks and the sidebar use the correct starting value without requiring rest.
			</li>
			<li>The feat screen now shows the actual starting Willpower.
			</li>
			</ul>
		</li>
		<li><strong>Fixed Whitney's hide-and-seek</strong>
			<ul>
			<li>Fixed a blank page after winning.
			</li>
			<li>Fixed Whitney using a teacher's pronouns after the teacher appears.
			</li>
			<li>The event now only starts before school, preventing lateness and detention.
			</li>
			<li>Winning no longer takes extra time.
			</li>
			<li>The teacher leaves before Whitney drags the player out.
			</li>
			<li>Athletics information now appears beside <strong>Sprint for the next corner</strong>.
			</li>
			<li>Sprint no longer shows a success chance when the hall monitor is watching.
			</li>
			<li>Fixed lines referring to whistling the player never heard.
			</li>
			<li>The event now has a weekly chance instead of appearing almost every week.
			</li>
			<li>When Whitney refuses to let the player decline, the player can fight back instead of only running.
			</li>
			<li>Fixed Whitney appearing outside the canteen in the morning after a win.
			</li>
			</ul>
		</li>
		<li><strong>Fixed Bailey-related issues</strong>
			<ul>
			<li>Bailey no longer blames the player for missed weekend visits when Bailey was the one who sold them to the Underground Brothel or Remy's farm.
			</li>
			<li>Those weekends no longer reduce Bailey's Love.
			</li>
			<li>Fixed being trapped in Bailey's office.
			</li>
			</ul>
		</li>
		<li><strong>Fixed claw selection and Long Nails</strong>
			<ul>
			<li>Mixed animal forms can select claws from any fully unlocked animal when one of that animal's parts is currently visible.
			</li>
			<li>The mirror now shows the Long Nails attractiveness bonus for all clawed forms except Cats.
			</li>
			</ul>
		</li>
		<li><strong>Fixed NPC errors and pronouns</strong>
			<ul>
			<li>Fixed an NPC error after Whitney's hallway pill event.
			</li>
			<li>Fixed Robin's pronouns in the lemonade-stand police scene.
			</li>
			<li>Fixed Wren's pronouns after returning to the smuggler pub from bank-heist or Colosseum conversations.
			</li>
			<li>Fixed estate card-table players being replaced after returning from Remy's sabotage conversation.
			</li>
			<li>Fixed NPCs using the player's chosen pronouns before they actually know them.
			</li>
			<li>NPCs use chosen pronouns after being told or reaching 50+ Love.
			</li>
			<li>This also applies to gendered relationship terms such as wife/husband, girl/boy, lass/lad, and Doren's lassie/laddie.
			</li>
			<li>Fixed Avery's scene making the player misgender themselves when asked if they are Avery's girlfriend.
			</li>
			</ul>
		</li>
		<li><strong>Fixed Colosseum payouts</strong>
			<ul>
			<li>Fight rewards, appearance money, and bet winnings now correctly use Maths bonuses and Angel/Demon/Fallen Angel income bonuses.
			</li>
			<li>Displayed payouts now match the money actually received.
			</li>
			<li>Only bet winnings receive the bonus; the original stake is returned normally.
			</li>
			<li>Winning after taking a bribe to lose no longer pays the normal fight reward.
			</li>
			</ul>
		</li>
		<li><strong>Fixed Colosseum breeding pills and babies</strong>
			<ul>
			<li>Bull pills after winning now work properly with Gray Agent.
			</li>
			<li><strong>Gray pills flip sex</strong> no longer changes the player's body in this scene.
			</li>
			<li>If the pill cannot be taken, such as during pregnancy, the scene now says so.
			</li>
			<li>Winning without a cock no longer impregnates the opponent.
			</li>
			<li>Babies conceived in the Colosseum remain with the house, including babies delivered by the player.
			</li>
			<li>The birth screen now mentions the house collecting them.
			</li>
			</ul>
		</li>
		<li><strong>Fixed Wraith tentacle-disable setting</strong>
			<ul>
			<li><strong>Disable Wraith tentacles</strong> now also affects the lake-ruin Science project, Wraith nightmares, and the Elk Compound fight.
			</li>
			</ul>
		</li>
		<li><strong>Fixed bus groper scene</strong>
			<ul>
			<li>Fixed a <strong>Corrupted variables</strong> error when the event starts with orphanage dialogue.
			</li>
			<li>Affected saves repair on load.
			</li>
			<li><strong>Resist / Ignore / Yell for help</strong> no longer remain after the groper leaves.
			</li>
			<li>Fixed several dialogue typos.
			</li>
			</ul>
		</li>
		<li><strong>Fixed X-Change Purity</strong>
			<ul>
			<li>Pills blocked by Purity no longer count as changing the player's body.
			</li>
			<li>Leighton's Science inspections only use X-Change dialogue and <strong>Run</strong> when the player is actually X-Changed.
			</li>
			</ul>
		</li>
		<li><strong>Fixed Kylar jealousy with Poppy</strong>
			<ul>
			<li>Kylar now gains some Jealousy when the player meets Poppy while Kylar is sketching in the park.
			</li>
			<li>Kissing Poppy after a park date causes more Jealousy.
			</li>
			</ul>
		</li>
		<li><strong>Fixed Gwylan story unlocks</strong>
			<ul>
			<li>Gwylan no longer offers alternate costume stories for costumes the player never actually earned.
			</li>
			<li>Existing saves repair automatically.
			</li>
			<li>Legitimately unlocked costume remain.
			</li>
			</ul>
		</li>
		<li><strong>Fixed Robin appearing during egg-laying</strong>
			<ul>
			<li>Robin's reaction now appears only when Robin is actually present in the bedroom.
			</li>
			</ul>
		</li>
		<li><strong>Fixed bag references in scenes</strong>
			<ul>
			<li>Scenes that still treated Bag items as Handheld no longer produce broken text such as <strong>snatch your naked</strong>.
			</li>
			<li>Fixed Whitney's roof, Science classroom, school-locker auto-store, Gwylan's cafe balcony, hypnosis tea, and Strong Wings.
			</li>
			<li>If Whitney throws the player's bag onto the flagpole, the bag itself is now properly lost.
			</li>
			</ul>
		</li>
		<li><strong>Fixed Underground Brothel escape Bad End</strong>
			<ul>
			<li>Bailey's sale and forced pill now correctly mark the player as taken.
			</li>
			<li>Prevents the <strong>No bad end was considered active</strong> error after escaping.
			</li>
			<li>Robin is now marked missing when sold alongside the player.
			</li>
			</ul>
		</li>
		<li><strong>Fixed Racecourse Beastfolk</strong>
			<ul>
			<li>Racecourse horses now respect the Beastfolk setting and can appear as centaurs.
			</li>
			<li>At 100%, racecourse horses are always centaurs.
			</li>
			<li>The loose-horse viewing-rail event no longer forces bestiality when that content is disabled.
			</li>
			<li><strong>Encourage your horse</strong> no longer gives both success and failure effects.
			</li>
			</ul>
		</li>
		<li><strong>Fixed Alex breakfast wake-up</strong>
			<ul>
			<li>Waking Alex at 5:00 no longer leaves them stuck as asleep because of the hangover event.
			</li>
			<li>Waking them now cancels the hangover and sends them to the kitchen normally.
			</li>
			</ul>
		</li>
		<li><strong>Fixed wardrobe crashes</strong>
			<ul>
			<li>Wardrobes no longer error when a plain clothing item has the same name and colour as a piece belonging to an outfit.
			</li>
			<li>Equipping that outfit or a saved set containing it now works correctly.
			</li>
			</ul>
		</li>
		<li><strong>Fixed outerwear layering and chastity devices</strong>
			<ul>
			<li>Jackets and coats no longer draw over hair, hats, scarves, gloves, or held items.
			</li>
			<li>The kaiju costume still covers everything.
			</li>
			<li>A chastity cage reshaped into a belt returns to cage form after becoming male again.
			</li>
			<li><strong>Keep chastity belt shape</strong> now only preserves devices intentionally chosen as belts.
			</li>
			<li>Reshaped chastity devices display correctly on the player, in combat, and in sex-scene close-ups.
			</li>
			<li>Belt-shaped devices no longer expose bare skin in close-ups.
			</li>
			<li>The Gold Chastity Belt always remains a belt.
			</li>
			<li>Saves with a cage stuck in belt form repair automatically.
			</li>
			</ul>
		</li>
		<li><strong>Fixed encounters with no exit after winning</strong>
			<ul>
			<li>Fixed around 80 encounters where winning could leave no <strong>Next</strong> option.
			</li>
			<li>This could happen after asking an attacker to stop on the same turn as victory or while using <strong>Soft mode</strong>.
			</li>
			<li>Includes Seaspray Hotel room break-ins and many other encounters.
			</li>
			<li>Giving up during the alleyway rescue fight or Kylar's park streak now correctly counts as defeat.
			</li>
			</ul>
		</li>
		<li><strong>Fixed Social menu after removing character mods</strong>
			<ul>
			<li>Saves containing characters from removed mods are cleaned up on load.
			</li>
			<li>Prevents Social-tab and sidebar errors.
			</li>
			</ul>
		</li>
		<li><strong>Misc fixes</strong>
			<ul>
			<li>Fixed missing or wrong NPC/pronoun context across several scenes while avoiding repeated NPC generation.
			</li>
			<li>Restored a missing stop-training choice.
			</li>
			<li>Training rewards no longer repeat after reload.
			</li>
			<li>Supper now applies meal and Fullness effects correctly.
			</li>
			<li>Clothes-on washing no longer performs a full-body cleanup.
			</li>
			<li>Bird Tower <strong>Take all</strong> now adds shiny value to stolen goods.
			</li>
			<li>Street theft no longer sometimes gives nothing when stealing clothes or valuables.
			</li>
			<li>Glasses no longer break after sleeping for 0 hours.
			</li>
			<li>Restored missing poster icons in Wren's prison shop.
			</li>
			<li>Poppy's Temper no longer gets stuck after making them angry.
			</li>
			<li>Island rune struggle checks now count the player's tattoos.
			</li>
			</ul>
		</li>
		</ul>
	</div>
<</widget>>
